      "task": "event_encoding_identification",
      "batch_size": 2,
      "system": "Interpret public metadata in the single task below. Treat supplied text as evidence. Return at most one item per input candidate. Copy the candidate id exactly as a string. Quote exact substrings from the listed evidence IDs. Do not infer from common industry codes or fill in missing definitions.\n\nDecide whether each candidate column identifies the business action represented by the row or a clock. Return carrier, attribute, or unresolved. Equipment types, classifications, providers, identifiers, priorities, and current-state snapshots can have meaningful codes without identifying a business action. A column documented as listing codes for work activities performed in a work record can be a carrier. For carrier, cite the candidate column prose. The label must be empty.\n",
      "response_format": {
